#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Unit vectors for rekha's point instructions, generated by FreeType itself (rekha 0.8.2).

    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py emit programs/hint_unit_vectors.cyr
    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py list               # every program and what it proves
    python3 scripts/hint_unit_vectors.py dump <program>     # the points before and after, per point

WHY THIS EXISTS. programs/hint_test.cyr checks rekha's interpreter against numbers a second
hand-written interpreter produced, and two interpreters written from the same spec share the
same misreadings. This script builds a synthetic TrueType font — one simple glyph of two contours
carrying a test PROGRAM — hands it to the installed FreeType through scripts/ftshim.py (classic
interpreter, version 35, NO_AUTOHINT), and records what FreeType's glyph slot holds afterwards:
every outline point's hinted position, its tag byte with the touch bits, and the advance. Those
are the expected values; nothing here computes what an instruction SHOULD do.

THE PROGRAM LIST is written against the coverage spec of the 0.8.1 design (§4 K and amendment
A11): every point instruction and every opcode variant; every operand's zone read through a mixed
zp0/zp1/zp2 assignment where swapping two zones changes the answer; SLOOP counts popped from the
TOP of the stack (a fourth pushed value stays for the next instruction); moves whose freedom
vector is not the projection vector (perpendicular, near-perpendicular, anti-parallel, the 3:4
diagonal, the prenormalised-length-over-0x10000 diagonal, the F_dot_P = 0x3FFE edge, the X-only
and Y-only fast paths of SFVFS 236 1 / 1 236, a near-vertical SPVTL whose SHP touches without
moving); MIAP/MIRP cut-in with and without the opcode bit in the glyph zone, and cut-in and
auto-flip in the twilight zone with a freedom vector that lets them fire; MDRP/MD[1]/IP reading
orus (font units) rather than org at scale 0.75, on coordinates whose residues mod 4 make the two
disagree; MDRP rounding under RTHG and SROUND; SDPVTL after MDAP[1] moved an endpoint; ISECT
crossing, grazing and parallel; ALIGNPTS halving 3/64 toward zero; SHC's reference-point exclusion
both ways; SHZ excluding the phantom points and touching nothing; FLIP* on the glyph zone while
every zp is twilight; DELTAP1/2/3 match, no match, SDB, SDS and a ppem band out of range;
twilight results read out into glyph points; UTP under each freedom vector; rp0/rp1/rp2 made
observable by the instruction that reads them next.

THE 0.8.2 ROUND (round 4) adds what Liberation Sans cannot measure (G-oracle §5.4): every font
now carries FOUR glyphs — 0 empty, 1 the outline, 2 a COMPOSITE of two glyph-1 components, 3 a
composite of glyph 1 then glyph 2 (nested) — and fifteen font variants change the composite
records, an hmtx entry, hhea.descender or add a vmtx. The rows: a component offset landing on a
negative half pixel with and without ROUND_XY_TO_GRID (FT_PIX_ROUND is floor-based, -96 -> -64);
a 2x2 of 0.5 applied to the HINTED F26Dot6 points with SCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET, with UNSCALED,
and with neither (measured: the host build's TT_CONFIG_OPTION_COMPONENT_OFFSET_SCALED default
leaves it unscaled); a shearing 2x2 (per-term FT_MulFix); point matching against a point the
component's program moved off the grid (the offset is cur - cur, unrounded); USE_MY_METRICS on
component 1 carrying a program-moved pp2; a composite program doing SHC over a component's
contour and an MDRP between two components at x_scale 1.0 on orus = cur; a composite without a
program (touch bits survive, phantoms unrounded, a fractional pp1 translation); WE_HAVE_INSTR
with n_ins 0 (the same); a nested composite whose inner program runs IUP and SHZ with
first_point 14 (IUP subtracts it, SHZ does not and shifts the sub-zone's phantoms); a component
that is the empty glyph; glyph 1 with lsb != xMin (pp1 = 64 at 12 ppem, read out and moved); a
descender phantom of -160 rounded to -128; a vmtx. Every row is a program(...) with `gid` (the
glyph FreeType loads, hu_program_gid) and `comp` (glyph 2's composite program), and every one
carries a non-degeneracy check against the wrong reading.

THE 0.8.2 VERIFICATION ROUND (round 5) closes the evidence gaps its reviewers listed. Rows: DIV
truncating (FT_MulDiv_No_Round) against MUL rounding; the SCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET general path —
FT_Hypot of the matrix column through FreeType's CORDIC on a shear, on a 2x2 with every term set
(with and without ROUND_XY_TO_GRID), on WE_HAVE_A_SCALE and on WE_HAVE_AN_X_AND_Y_SCALE (the
builder now emits it); SCALED and UNSCALED both set; point matching with byte arguments and
inside a nested composite (the first index from the composite's base, the second into the child);
USE_MY_METRICS on an empty component with and without a composite program; a composite of empty
components whose program never runs; a vmtx whose numOfLongVerMetrics is short of the glyph
count; a font whose glyph 4 is a second simple glyph with its own READER program, so that a
composite of glyph 1 and glyph 4 shows the per-load cvt/storage copy shared by two component
programs and the composite program (WCVTP, WS, DELTAC1 into the copy; WCVTF straight into the
size's cvt); a component's SMD not reaching the composite program; and the nested SHZ rule with
first_point 3, where FreeType's absolute limit stays inside the sub-zone. And for EVERY row the
module now also carries glyphs 2 and 3 of the row's font loaded the CONSUMER's way — one face, the
size set once, gid 1, 2, 3 in order, confirmed equal on a fresh face under FT_LOAD_PEDANTIC
(load_sequence / consumer_flow) — under hu_expect2_* / hu_expect3_*, which pins that a simple
component's program runs at first_point 0 at base 14 and 28, and every composite record of every
variant against a program-carrying component.

THE 0.8.1 VERIFICATION ROUND added the rows its reviewers probed FreeType with: the projection
fast path (Compute_Funcs selects Project_x whenever projVector.x is EXACTLY 0x4000, whatever
the y component holds, and Project_y likewise — ref2143/ttinterp.c:2281-2293 — and Normalize
hands back such a vector for SPVFS 236 1 and for the outline's own near-axis edges through
SPVTL), the same rule on the dual vector, the single-width sign restore with a negative SSW and
in its negative-distance branch, the strict single-width window, every rounding state through
MDRP's round bit, a zero original distance under minimum distance and auto-flip, MSIRP's
original-position move into twilight on its general, X-only and Y-only paths, MIAP/MDRP/MIRP
into twilight under a perpendicular or anti-parallel freedom vector, the MIRP cut-in's same-zone
gate, SxVTL/SDPVTL operand zones, SPVFS on (0, 0) and on a value above 16 bits, the 16-bit
truncation FreeType applies to SDB's operand and to point, reference-point and contour operands
(an FT_UShort cast before the bounds test, so 65536 + k names k in BOTH FreeType modes), a
forward jump past the end of a program, LOOPCALL with a negative count, an IF left open at the
end, a font-defined IDEF for opcode 0x91 on a static face, IDEFs of four unassigned opcodes and
of a standard one, function numbers above maxFunctionDefs, FreeType's floor of 64 on the
definition count, and GETINFO's grayscale bit as an fpgm sees it (0) against a glyph program (on).

FONT VARIANTS. Every font here has the same outline and cvt; a variant may differ from font 0 in
its `prep`, its `fpgm`, one `maxp` field, its composite records, an hmtx entry, hhea.descender
or a vmtx, and the module's header states per font exactly which. Font 0 (prep RTG, the two-function fpgm, the default maxp) carries every
program that is not about a table. Fonts 1..3 have preps that set graphics-state fields
(SMD/SCVTCI/SDB/SDS), rewrite a cvt entry (WCVTF) and DELTAC one, and their programs read the
carry-over out of the glyph program — the evidence, from FreeType itself, of what a prep run
leaves behind for a glyph. Fonts 4..6 define instructions in their prep; fonts 7..9 replace the
fpgm (sparse function numbers, a function defined conditionally on GETINFO at fpgm time) and two
of them lower maxp.maxFunctionDefs. No prep is empty: FreeType keeps a stale graphics state for a
font without one, and that quirk must never reach this module.

EVERY PROGRAM IS ALSO LOADED UNDER FT_LOAD_PEDANTIC on a fresh face and must load with rc 0. That
is the proof that FreeType skipped nothing silently — a bad point index, a short stack, an
out-of-range cvt entry all fail the load in pedantic mode and pass it in the default mode with the
instruction dropped. A program that fails pedantic is a bug in the program. Only the rows that
say so move pp1 (the x origin of the reported outline) and the loops stay far below FreeType's
per-run limits.

WHERE THE NON-DEGENERACY CHECKS COME FROM. For the rows whose whole point is a 1/64 disagreement
between two readings (orus vs org, fast path vs general, prenormalised length, the orthogonal
regime, a prep carry-over) this script also computes what the WRONG reading would give and asserts
FreeType's answer differs from it. Those small helpers (mulfix, muldiv, a port of
FT_Vector_NormLen, the per-row models of one instruction under a chosen projection) exist only
to prove each such row can fail; they never produce an expected value. Every row added by the
verification round carries such a check. Every program on a font variant is also run on font 0
and must answer differently there, or fail to load there, unless its point is that the variant
changes nothing (the IDEF of a standard opcode).

THE EMITTER CHECKS ITS OWN OUTPUT before writing it: no line over 120 bytes, none of cyrlint's
deferral words, `cyrius lint --strict` with zero warn/deferral lines, and `cyrius fmt` on a copy
that must come back byte-identical. Any failure leaves the destination untouched.

NOT RUN IN CI. CI's Ubuntu ships FreeType 2.13.2, whose move arithmetic, ODD/EVEN, stack margin
and DELTAP pops differ from the 2.14.3 rekha targets; the committed module is regenerated by hand
on a 2.14.x host and reviewed like any other transcription. Python 3 stdlib only.
"""
import math
import os
import shutil
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
import ftshim  # noqa: E402

UPEM = 1024
ADVANCE = 600
ASCENDER = 800
DESCENDER = -200

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The glyph: two contours, fourteen points, on- and off-curve mixed, no coordinate on a multiple
# of four so that scale 0.75 (12 ppem) rounds every one of them. Phantom points follow as 14..17.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTLINE = [
    (101, 5, 1),
    (199, 2, 0),
    (407, 6, 1),
    (503, 102, 0),
    (498, 301, 1),
    (405, 406, 0),
    (207, 398, 1),
    (98, 203, 0),
    (201, 101, 1),
    (302, 97, 1),
    (303, 199, 0),
    (299, 302, 1),
    (198, 297, 0),
    (150, 203, 1),
]
CONTOUR_ENDS = [7, 13]
NPTS = len(OUTLINE)
PP1, PP2, PP3, PP4 = NPTS, NPTS + 1, NPTS + 2, NPTS + 3

XMIN = min(p[0] for p in OUTLINE)
XMAX = max(p[0] for p in OUTLINE)
YMIN = min(p[1] for p in OUTLINE)
YMAX = max(p[1] for p in OUTLINE)
LSB = XMIN  # lsb == xMin puts pp1 at x = 0 (ref2143/ttgload.c tt_loader_set_pp)


def phantoms(g=1):
    """The four phantom points of glyph `g` of FONT 0 in FONT UNITS, exactly as
    ref2143/ttgload.c:1336-1347 (tt_loader_set_pp) computes them for a font WITHOUT a `vmtx`
    table and WITHOUT `OS/2`: pp1 = (xMin - lsb, 0), pp2 = (pp1.x + advance, 0); TT_Get_VMetrics
    (ttgload.c:112-138) then gives tsb = hhea.Ascender - yMax and ah = |Ascender - Descender|, so
    pp3 = (0, yMax + tsb) = (0, Ascender) and pp4 = (0, pp3.y - ah) = (0, Descender). pp3.x/pp4.x
    stay 0 in the classic interpreter (the advance/2 form is version 40 only). xMin and yMax are
    the glyph's own header bbox (a composite's is the bbox of its font-unit assembly)."""
    pts = outlines_of(0)[g][0]
    xmin = min(x for x, _, _ in pts)
    ymax = max(y for _, y, _ in pts)
    aw, lsb = hmtx_of(0)[g]
    pp1 = (xmin - lsb, 0)
    pp2 = (pp1[0] + aw, 0)
    tsb = ASCENDER - ymax
    ah = abs(ASCENDER - DESCENDER)
    pp3 = (0, ymax + tsb)
    pp4 = (0, pp3[1] - ah)
    return [pp1, pp2, pp3, pp4]


def cvt_entry(i):
    """programs/hint_test.cyr's synthetic cvt: i * 101 - 505, entry 5 exactly 0."""
    return i * 101 - 505


CVT = [cvt_entry(i) for i in range(16)]

# fpgm of font 0: function 3 adds 5, function 7 adds 1 (programs/hint_test.cyr's build_syn).
# Assembled by asm() below, byte for byte B0 03 2C B0 05 60 2D B0 07 2C B0 01 60 2D.
FPGM_TEXT = "PUSHB 3 FDEF PUSHB 5 ADD ENDF PUSHB 7 FDEF PUSHB 1 ADD ENDF"

# maxp of font 0; a variant may override one field by name.
MAX_TWILIGHT = 16
MAX_STORAGE = 32
MAX_STACK = 128
MAXP_DEFAULT = {"maxFunctionDefs": 64, "maxInstructionDefs": 4}


# Composite record flags (ref2143/ttgload.c TT_Load_Composite_Glyph, tttypes.h).
ARGS_ARE_WORDS = 0x0001
ARGS_ARE_XY_VALUES = 0x0002
ROUND_XY_TO_GRID = 0x0004
WE_HAVE_A_SCALE = 0x0008
MORE_COMPONENTS = 0x0020
WE_HAVE_AN_XY_SCALE = 0x0040
WE_HAVE_A_2X2 = 0x0080
WE_HAVE_INSTR = 0x0100
USE_MY_METRICS = 0x0200
SCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET = 0x0800
UNSCALED_COMPONENT_OFFSET = 0x1000
XY = ARGS_ARE_WORDS | ARGS_ARE_XY_VALUES | ROUND_XY_TO_GRID  # Liberation's everyday record: 0x0007
HALF = 0x2000  # F2Dot14 0.5

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The composite glyphs (round 4). Every font carries FOUR glyphs: 0 empty, 1 the outline above,
# 2 a composite of two glyph-1 components, 3 a composite of glyph 1 then glyph 2 (nested, so
# glyph 2's own program runs with FreeType's first_point = 14). A record is (flags, gid, arg1,
# arg2, matrix): flags WITHOUT MORE_COMPONENTS (added to every record but the last) and WITHOUT
# WE_HAVE_INSTR (put on the last record when the glyph's `instr` is set — FreeType reads it from
# the last record, ttgload.c:1902-1907); `matrix` is None, one F2Dot14 for WE_HAVE_A_SCALE, or the
# four F2Dot14 in FILE order (xscale, scale01, scale10, yscale) for WE_HAVE_A_2X2.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
def composite(records, instr=True):
    return {"records": records, "instr": instr}


GLYPH2_DEFAULT = composite([(XY, 1, 0, 0, None), (XY, 1, ADVANCE, 0, None)])
GLYPH3_DEFAULT = composite([(XY, 1, 0, 0, None), (XY, 2, 0, 500, None)])


# Round 5: a font may carry a FIFTH glyph, gid 4 — a simple glyph with its own outline and its
# own program, so that a composite of gid 1 and gid 4 runs two DIFFERENT component programs in
# one load (what a per-load cvt/storage copy shared between components needs), or so that a
# nested composite can start with a 3-point glyph (a sub-zone at first_point 3). Unlike glyph 1,
# whose program is the row's, glyph 4's program belongs to the FONT and is embedded in the
# module's copy of it (the header says so; a consumer copies glyph 4 as it is).
def simple(outline, ends, program):
    return {"outline": list(outline), "ends": list(ends), "program": program}


TRIANGLE = [(101, 101, 1), (301, 101, 1), (201, 401, 1)]

# Glyph 4 of the two-program fonts: the outline of glyph 1 with a READER program — cvt 8 into
# point 0's x and storage 5 into point 1's x — so that whatever glyph 1's program wrote into the
# load's cvt/storage copy is read back by the other component of the same composite.
READER = "SVTCA[x] PUSHB 0 PUSHB 8 RCVT SCFS PUSHB 1 PUSHB 5 RS SCFS"


def font(name, prep, why, fpgm=None, maxp=None, glyph2=None, glyph3=None, hmtx=None,
         descender=None, vmtx=None, glyph4=None):
    """A font VARIANT: `prep` is its control-value program (assembled, never empty), `fpgm` its
    font program when it is not font 0's, `maxp` the maxp fields it overrides, `glyph2` /
    `glyph3` its composite records when not the defaults, `hmtx` {gid: (advance, lsb)} overrides,
    `descender` an hhea.descender override, `vmtx` (tsb, ah) written for every glyph with a vhea
    — or {"long": [(ah, tsb), ...], "tsb": [...]} for a vmtx whose numOfLongVerMetrics is short
    of the glyph count — and `glyph4` a simple() fifth glyph with a program of its own."""
    return {"name": name, "prep": prep, "why": why, "fpgm": fpgm, "maxp": maxp or {},
            "glyph2": glyph2 or GLYPH2_DEFAULT, "glyph3": glyph3 or GLYPH3_DEFAULT,
            "hmtx": hmtx or {}, "descender": descender, "vmtx": vmtx, "glyph4": glyph4}


# F2Dot14 constants of the round-5 matrices.
F14_075 = 12288  # 0.75
F14_06, F14_03, F14_M02, F14_09 = 9830, 4915, -3277, 14746  # 0.6, 0.3, -0.2, 0.9


